course: dictionary
lesson: 12372
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one is right. «The young prince was crowned king in the great hall.» A crown goes on a king's head, so here crowned means had a crown placed on the head to become king.
explain: «Maya was crowned champion after the final race.» No crown is needed here. The winner was officially named the best, so crowned means chosen as the winner. The words champion and race are the clues.
explain: «Snow crowned the top of the hill.» Here crowned means covered at the top, like a crown sitting on a head. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have found the right one.
fact: Crowned is the past tense of crown, so it describes something that has already happened.
fact: «Crowned» can mean had a crown placed on the head to become king or queen.
fact: «Crowned» can mean officially named the winner or best, as in «crowned champion».
fact: «Crowned» can also mean covered at the top, as in «a hill crowned with snow».
fact: When a word has several meanings, the other words in the sentence show you which meaning to use.
exercise: «The team was crowned champions after winning every game.» What does crowned mean here? | Fell over at the end | Covered at the top | *Officially named the winners | Had a crown put on its head
exercise: «The old castle was crowned with towers.» What does crowned mean? | Hidden underground | *Topped or covered at the top | Made into a king | Named the best castle in the land
exercise: «The king was crowned in a grand ceremony.» Find and copy the word that tells you a crown was put on his head. | grand | king | *crowned | ceremony
test: «The king was crowned at the age of ten.» What does crowned mean? | *Had a crown placed on his head to become king | Fell down from a high place | Was given a prize for drawing
test: Which meaning fits «The hill was crowned with snow»? | *Covered at the top | Named the winner of the hill | Crowned as a king of the snow
exam: In «Mo was crowned champion of the chess club», what does crowned mean? | Tired and sleepy | *Officially named the best | Covered at the top | Put a crown on his head
